{"version":"1","id":"98629eef-43c9-42d9-915a-0ceda8bc8bc7","handle":"c_community","name":"C/C++ Community","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--pmYey7LF--/f_auto/v1731952415/squads/98629eef-43c9-42d9-915a-0ceda8bc8bc7","description":null,"is_squad":true,"x":-9.2142,"y":9.7755,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":17,"newest_post_at":"2026-04-18T19:20:10.746Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-09-27T19:30:52.217Z","features":{"hype_score":0.058824,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.588235,"summary_length_avg":348.235294,"title_length_avg":47.941176,"title_length_var":627.937716,"tag_entropy":2.850001,"tag_diversity":1.411765,"top_tag_share":0.294118,"avg_upvotes":6.882353,"median_upvotes":5.0,"avg_comments":2.294118,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.338983,"zero_engagement_share":0.058824,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.20951,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"recency_skew":0.307692},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[5.9853,9.8529],"cadence_depth":[-8.6765,-8.2794],"hype_variety":[8.5294,-3.5],"title_style":[-9.0588,-8.4265]},"top_tags":[["c++",7],["c",7],["open-source",6],["lua",6],["linux",4],["compiler",3],["qt",3],["kernel-development",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["\ud83d\udd27 Kernel Development with C++","Just released Rhythm v2.0.0","\ud83d\ude80 Built a Neural Network Library in C++ from Scratch - Here's What I Learned About the Fundamentals Behind ML Frameworks"],"outlier":["Jet brains"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"sH0dF2kic","title":"Online talk about creating a C++ based custom language and lexer internals","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/online-talk-about-creating-a-c-based-custom-language-and-lexer-internals-sh0df2kic","summary":"PVS-Studio developers are hosting an online talk as part of their series on building a custom programming language in C++. This session focuses on the lexer: what it is, its components, and how to work with it.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--3kWQKotY--/f_auto/v1776431687/posts/RKgpuTNNM?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-18T19:20:10.746Z"},{"id":"UTPpQLkeS","title":"Tpool - A Thread pool library written in C","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tpool---a-thread-pool-library-written-in-c-utppqlkes","summary":"A developer shares Tpool, a thread pool library written in C using pthreads, mutex, and condition variables with a circular buffer and FIFO scheduling. The post covers a benchmark experiment sorting a ~4GB integer array with concurrent recursive quicksort calls using 6 worker threads vs single-threaded execution, achieving a 67% performance improvement (14.5s vs 43.4s). A notable deadlock bug is discussed where consumers acting as producers caused all threads to wait indefinitely. Future plans include implementing a lock-free work-stealing deque for further performance gains.","image":null,"num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2026-04-01T08:11:05.617Z"},{"id":"jIOrQezKT","title":"Neat compile-time sizeof trick for embedded systems","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/neat-compile-time-sizeof-trick-for-embedded-systems-jiorqezkt","summary":"A clever C trick for embedded systems where printf isn't available: use duplicate case values in a switch statement with sizeof() to force the compiler to reveal struct sizes at compile time via a duplicate case error message.","image":null,"num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2026-03-29T16:27:04.728Z"},{"id":"fBImeg6ul","title":"Arrays: The Self-Contained Algorithmic Universe in C++","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/arrays-the-self-contained-algorithmic-universe-in-c--fbimeg6ul","summary":"Arrays in C++ are presented as a self-contained algorithmic universe that independently generates three core technique families: indexing and traversal skeletons (sliding window, two-pointer, binary search), coordinate transformations (transpose, rotation, mirroring), and partitioning strategies (divide-and-conquer, merge sort, quicksort). Unlike other C++ concepts that require combining with external ideas, arrays alone provide a complete toolkit for algorithmic problem-solving, making them both a beginner entry point and an advanced developer's foundation.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-20T19:40:52.667Z"},{"id":"FcQZWKzai","title":"Built an HTTP server in C using Mongoose - a tiny, embeddable web server.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/built-an-http-server-in-c-using-mongoose---a-tiny-embeddable-web-server--fcqzwkzai","summary":"Learn how to build production-ready HTTP servers in C using Mongoose, an embedded networking library. The guide covers creating both static file servers and dynamic RESTful API servers with minimal code, demonstrating C's performance capabilities for web server development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--esaAAt7D--/f_auto/v1760107661/posts/FcQZWKzai?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-10-10T14:47:41.750Z"},{"id":"ChZAmjTPY","title":"Released Loom v1.2.1 Beta \u2013 File Tree Viewer Update!","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/released-loom-v1-2-1-beta-file-tree-viewer-update--chzamjtpy","summary":"Loom v1.2.1 Beta introduces a major update featuring a file tree viewer with project navigation, multiple theme support (Gruvbox, Dracula, Catppuccin Mocha), and enhanced plugin system. The lightweight text editor offers syntax highlighting for multiple languages, Lua-based configuration, and built-in plugins for auto-saving and formatting. Currently Linux-only with Qt5 dependencies.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--swd8HYj0--/f_auto/v1756954600/posts/ChZAmjTPY?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-09-04T02:56:40.081Z"},{"id":"L3Filgdie","title":"Released Loom v1.1.0 Beta \u2013 major update","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/released-loom-v1-1-0-beta-major-update-l3filgdie","summary":"Loom v1.1.0 Beta introduces a major update to the lightweight text editor with new theme switching capabilities (Gruvbox, Dracula, Catppuccin Mocha), enhanced plugin system with dynamic menu updates, and improved user experience. The release includes built-in plugins for theme switching, auto-save, and auto-formatting with support for multiple programming languages. Available for Linux systems with Qt5 and Lua dependencies.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--lA6adAbx--/f_auto/v1756738760/posts/L3Filgdie?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-09-01T14:59:20.120Z"},{"id":"ONIxGDsd3","title":"Released Loom v1.0.0 Beta - a fast, minimal text editor.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/released-loom-v1-0-0-beta---a-fast-minimal-text-editor--onixgdsd3","summary":"Loom v1.0.0 Beta is a lightweight text editor built with C++ and Qt, weighing only 4.2MB. It features Gruvbox theming, Lua scripting support for plugins, syntax highlighting, multi-tab interface, and auto-formatting capabilities while maintaining minimal resource usage.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZEKt_yZW--/f_auto/v1756685323/posts/ONIxGDsd3?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2025-09-01T00:08:43.072Z"},{"id":"GESoPKiLK","title":"Just released Rhythm v2.0.0","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/just-released-rhythm-v2-0-0-gesopkilk","summary":"Rhythm v2.0.0 has been released as a lightweight music visualizer application built with C and Lua using the Love2D framework. The software is available as a .deb package under 2.5MB and is open source, welcoming community contributions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--7Bkdk568--/f_auto/v1756135781/posts/GESoPKiLK?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":20,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2025-08-25T15:29:41.108Z"},{"id":"GZqXmA4zN","title